Based on my research, the latest MSTest is **4.2.3**. Here are the breaking changes relevant to **your project**:

---

## 🚨 `[ExpectedException]` is removed in MSTest 4

This is the main breaking change affecting your code. The `ExpectedExceptionAttribute` was deprecated and is now completely removed. You must replace it with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()`.

**Before (your current code):**
```csharp
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}
```

**After:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

---

## ⚠️ Other changes to be aware of

| Change | Impact on your project |
|--------|----------------------|
| `Assert` APIs no longer accept `message` + `params object[]` — use string interpolation | Low (you don't use messages) |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | None (not used) |
| Analyzer MSTEST0032 upgraded to **Warning** | `Assert.IsTrue(true)` will now warn |
| Minimum TFM is .NET 8+ | ✅ You're already on net8.0 |
| Many internal types hidden | Unlikely to affect you |

---

## Fix summary

Update your `.csproj`:
```xml
<PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="4.2.3" />
```

Update your test methods to replace `[ExpectedException]`:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}

[TestMethod]
public void Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<InvalidOperationException>(() => Process());
}
```

And consider fixing the `Assert.IsTrue(true)` (MSTEST0032 warning) by replacing it with a meaningful assertion.

Would you like me to apply these changes to your project?
